('a15d2915-ab75-5147-b69e-83ffb90778de'::uuid, 8, 23, 333, 333, 'यत्र काले त्वनावृत्तिमावृत्तिं चैव योगिनः।

प्रयाता यान्ति तं कालं वक्ष्यामि भरतर्षभ।।8.23।।', 'yatra kāle tvanāvṛittim āvṛittiṁ chaiva yoginaḥ
prayātā yānti taṁ kālaṁ vakṣhyāmi bharatarṣhabha', '[{"word":"yatra","meaning":"where"},{"word":"kāle","meaning":"time"},{"word":"tu","meaning":"certainly"},{"word":"anāvṛittim","meaning":"no return"},{"word":"āvṛittim","meaning":"return"},{"word":"cha","meaning":"and"},{"word":"eva","meaning":"certainly"},{"word":"yoginaḥ","meaning":"a yogi"},{"word":"prayātāḥ","meaning":"having departed"},{"word":"yānti","meaning":"attain"},{"word":"tam","meaning":"that"},{"word":"kālam","meaning":"time"},{"word":"vakṣhyāmi","meaning":"I shall describe"},{"word":"bharata","meaning":"ṛiṣhabha—Arjun, the best of the Bharatas"}]'::jsonb, 'yatra—where; kāle—time; tu—certainly; anāvṛittim—no return; āvṛittim—return; cha—and; eva—certainly; yoginaḥ—a yogi; prayātāḥ—having departed; yānti—attain; tam—that; kālam—time; vakṣhyāmi—I shall describe; bharata-ṛiṣhabha—Arjun, the best of the Bharatas;'),
('46e0ee3c-ed51-5493-9e72-24f889d6ad5e'::uuid, 8, 24, 334, 334, 'अग्निर्ज्योतिरहः शुक्लः षण्मासा उत्तरायणम्।

तत्र प्रयाता गच्छन्ति ब्रह्म ब्रह्मविदो जनाः।।8.24।।', 'agnir jyotir ahaḥ śhuklaḥ ṣhaṇ-māsā uttarāyaṇam
tatra prayātā gachchhanti brahma brahma-vido janāḥ', '[{"word":"agniḥ","meaning":"fire"},{"word":"jyotiḥ","meaning":"light"},{"word":"ahaḥ","meaning":"day"},{"word":"śhuklaḥ","meaning":"the bright fortnight of the moon"},{"word":"ṣhaṭ","meaning":"māsāḥ—six months"},{"word":"uttara","meaning":"ayanam—the sun’s northern course"},{"word":"tatra","meaning":"there"},{"word":"prayātāḥ","meaning":"departed"},{"word":"gachchhanti","meaning":"go"},{"word":"brahma","meaning":"Brahman"},{"word":"brahma","meaning":"vidaḥ—those who know the Brahman"},{"word":"janāḥ","meaning":"persons"}]'::jsonb, 'agniḥ—fire; jyotiḥ—light; ahaḥ—day; śhuklaḥ—the bright fortnight of the moon; ṣhaṭ-māsāḥ—six months; uttara-ayanam—the sun’s northern course; tatra—there; prayātāḥ—departed; gachchhanti—go; brahma—Brahman; brahma-vidaḥ—those who know the Brahman; janāḥ—persons;'),
('c1a256da-a274-55bd-9628-73e55c1d39ca'::uuid, 8, 25, 335, 335, 'धूमो रात्रिस्तथा कृष्णः षण्मासा दक्षिणायनम्।

तत्र चान्द्रमसं ज्योतिर्योगी प्राप्य निवर्तते।।8.25।।', 'dhūmo rātris tathā kṛiṣhṇaḥ ṣhaṇ-māsā dakṣhiṇāyanam
tatra chāndramasaṁ jyotir yogī prāpya nivartate', '[{"word":"dhūmaḥ","meaning":"smoke"},{"word":"rātriḥ","meaning":"night"},{"word":"tathā","meaning":"and"},{"word":"kṛiṣhṇaḥ","meaning":"the dark fortnight of the moon"},{"word":"ṣhaṭ","meaning":"māsāḥ—six months"},{"word":"dakṣhiṇa","meaning":"ayanam—the sun’s southern course"},{"word":"tatra","meaning":"there"},{"word":"chāndra","meaning":"masam—lunar"},{"word":"jyotiḥ","meaning":"light"},{"word":"yogī","meaning":"a yogi"},{"word":"prāpya","meaning":"attain"},{"word":"nivartate","meaning":"comes back"}]'::jsonb, 'dhūmaḥ—smoke; rātriḥ—night; tathā—and; kṛiṣhṇaḥ—the dark fortnight of the moon; ṣhaṭ-māsāḥ—six months; dakṣhiṇa-ayanam—the sun’s southern course; tatra—there; chāndra-masam—lunar; jyotiḥ—light; yogī—a yogi; prāpya—attain; nivartate—comes back;'),
('82d794a7-e2da-5c17-bc6b-87f6850ef802'::uuid, 8, 26, 336, 336, 'शुक्लकृष्णे गती ह्येते जगतः शाश्वते मते।

एकया यात्यनावृत्तिमन्ययाऽऽवर्तते पुनः।।8.26।।', 'śhukla-kṛiṣhṇe gatī hyete jagataḥ śhāśhvate mate
ekayā yātyanāvṛittim anyayāvartate punaḥ', '[{"word":"śhukla","meaning":"bright"},{"word":"kṛiṣhṇe","meaning":"dark"},{"word":"gatī","meaning":"paths"},{"word":"hi","meaning":"certainly"},{"word":"ete","meaning":"these"},{"word":"jagataḥ","meaning":"of the material world"},{"word":"śhāśhvate","meaning":"eternal"},{"word":"mate","meaning":"opinion"},{"word":"ekayā","meaning":"by one"},{"word":"yāti","meaning":"goes"},{"word":"anāvṛittim","meaning":"to non return"},{"word":"anyayā","meaning":"by the other"},{"word":"āvartate","meaning":"comes back"},{"word":"punaḥ","meaning":"again"}]'::jsonb, 'śhukla—bright; kṛiṣhṇe—dark; gatī—paths; hi—certainly; ete—these; jagataḥ—of the material world; śhāśhvate—eternal; mate—opinion; ekayā—by one; yāti—goes; anāvṛittim—to non return; anyayā—by the other; āvartate—comes back; punaḥ—again'),
('64ecf1da-d332-5de6-9cc6-29542ebcdbd3'::uuid, 8, 27, 337, 337, 'नैते सृती पार्थ जानन्योगी मुह्यति कश्चन।

तस्मात्सर्वेषु कालेषु योगयुक्तो भवार्जुन।।8.27।।', 'naite sṛitī pārtha jānan yogī muhyati kaśhchana
