('7b0a4903-1a30-5580-bbbc-9c48ed82ad71'::uuid, 17, 1, 596, 596, 'अर्जुन उवाचये शास्त्रविधिमुत्सृज्य यजन्ते श्रद्धयाऽन्विताः।तेषां निष्ठा तु का कृष्ण सत्त्वमाहो रजस्तमः।।17.1।।', 'arjuna uvācha
ye śhāstra-vidhim utsṛijya yajante śhraddhayānvitāḥ
teṣhāṁ niṣhṭhā tu kā kṛiṣhṇa sattvam āho rajas tamaḥ', '[{"word":"arjunaḥ uvācha","meaning":"Arjun said"},{"word":"ye","meaning":"who"},{"word":"śhāstra","meaning":"vidhim—scriptural injunctions"},{"word":"utsṛijya","meaning":"disregard"},{"word":"yajante","meaning":"worship"},{"word":"śhraddhayā","meaning":"anvitāḥ—with faith"},{"word":"teṣhām","meaning":"their"},{"word":"niṣhṭhā","meaning":"faith"},{"word":"tu","meaning":"indeed"},{"word":"kā","meaning":"what"},{"word":"kṛiṣhṇa","meaning":"Krishna"},{"word":"sattvam","meaning":"mode of goodness"},{"word":"āho","meaning":"or"},{"word":"rajaḥ","meaning":"mode of passion"},{"word":"tamaḥ","meaning":"mode of ignorance"}]'::jsonb, 'arjunaḥ uvācha—Arjun said; ye—who; śhāstra-vidhim—scriptural injunctions; utsṛijya—disregard; yajante—worship; śhraddhayā-anvitāḥ—with faith; teṣhām—their; niṣhṭhā—faith; tu—indeed; kā—what; kṛiṣhṇa—Krishna; sattvam—mode of goodness; āho—or; rajaḥ—mode of passion; tamaḥ—mode of ignorance'),
('0d90172a-27f2-5682-83ec-f7c9c39230f7'::uuid, 17, 2, 597, 597, 'श्री भगवानुवाचत्रिविधा भवति श्रद्धा देहिनां सा स्वभावजा।सात्त्विकी राजसी चैव तामसी चेति तां श्रृणु।।17.2।।', 'śhrī-bhagavān uvācha
tri-vidhā bhavati śhraddhā dehināṁ sā svabhāva-jā
sāttvikī rājasī chaiva tāmasī cheti tāṁ śhṛiṇu', '[{"word":"śhrī","meaning":"bhagavān uvācha—the Supreme Personality said"},{"word":"tri","meaning":"vidhā—of three kinds"},{"word":"bhavati","meaning":"is"},{"word":"śhraddhā","meaning":"faith"},{"word":"dehinām","meaning":"embodied beings"},{"word":"sā","meaning":"which"},{"word":"sva","meaning":"bhāva-jā—born of one’s innate nature"},{"word":"sāttvikī","meaning":"of the mode of goodness"},{"word":"rājasī","meaning":"of the mode of passion"},{"word":"cha","meaning":"and"},{"word":"eva","meaning":"certainly"},{"word":"tāmasī","meaning":"of the mode of ignorance"},{"word":"cha","meaning":"and"},{"word":"iti","meaning":"thus"},{"word":"tām","meaning":"about this"},{"word":"śhṛiṇu","meaning":"hear"}]'::jsonb, 'śhrī-bhagavān uvācha—the Supreme Personality said; tri-vidhā—of three kinds; bhavati—is; śhraddhā—faith; dehinām—embodied beings; sā—which; sva-bhāva-jā—born of one’s innate nature; sāttvikī—of the mode of goodness; rājasī—of the mode of passion; cha—and; eva—certainly; tāmasī—of the mode of ignorance; cha—and; iti—thus; tām—about this; śhṛiṇu—hear'),
('2b285c7c-cb2f-516f-aa2b-1f5543ad6b62'::uuid, 17, 3, 598, 598, 'सत्त्वानुरूपा सर्वस्य श्रद्धा भवति भारत।श्रद्धामयोऽयं पुरुषो यो यच्छ्रद्धः स एव सः।।17.3।।', 'sattvānurūpā sarvasya śhraddhā bhavati bhārata
śhraddhā-mayo ‘yaṁ puruṣho yo yach-chhraddhaḥ sa eva saḥ', '[{"word":"sattva","meaning":"anurūpā—conforming to the nature of one’s mind"},{"word":"sarvasya","meaning":"all"},{"word":"śhraddhā","meaning":"faith"},{"word":"bhavati","meaning":"is"},{"word":"bhārata","meaning":"Arjun, the scion of Bharat"},{"word":"śhraddhāmayaḥ","meaning":"possessing faith"},{"word":"ayam","meaning":"that"},{"word":"puruṣhaḥ","meaning":"human being"},{"word":"yaḥ","meaning":"who"},{"word":"yat","meaning":"śhraddhaḥ—whatever the nature of their faith"},{"word":"saḥ","meaning":"their"},{"word":"eva","meaning":"verily"},{"word":"saḥ","meaning":"they"}]'::jsonb, 'sattva-anurūpā—conforming to the nature of one’s mind; sarvasya—all; śhraddhā—faith; bhavati—is; bhārata—Arjun, the scion of Bharat; śhraddhāmayaḥ—possessing faith; ayam—that; puruṣhaḥ—human being; yaḥ—who; yat-śhraddhaḥ—whatever the nature of their faith; saḥ—their; eva—verily; saḥ—they'),
('1e55bf10-c62e-519a-b980-62fa7c774ef8'::uuid, 17, 4, 599, 599, 'यजन्ते सात्त्विका देवान्यक्षरक्षांसि राजसाः।प्रेतान्भूतगणांश्चान्ये यजन्ते तामसा जनाः।।17.4।।', 'yajante sāttvikā devān yakṣha-rakṣhānsi rājasāḥ
pretān bhūta-gaṇānśh chānye yajante tāmasā janāḥ', '[{"word":"yajante","meaning":"worship"},{"word":"sāttvikāḥ","meaning":"those in the mode of goodness"},{"word":"devān","meaning":"celestial gods"},{"word":"yakṣha","meaning":"semi-celestial beings who exude power and wealth"},{"word":"rakṣhānsi","meaning":"powerful beings who embody sensual enjoyment, revenge, and wrath"},{"word":"rājasāḥ","meaning":"those in the mode of passion"},{"word":"pretān","meaning":"bhūta-gaṇān—ghosts and spirits"},{"word":"cha","meaning":"and"},{"word":"anye","meaning":"others"},{"word":"yajante","meaning":"worship"},{"word":"tāmasāḥ","meaning":"those in the mode of ignorance"},{"word":"janāḥ","meaning":"persons"}]'::jsonb, 'yajante—worship; sāttvikāḥ—those in the mode of goodness; devān—celestial gods; yakṣha—semi-celestial beings who exude power and wealth; rakṣhānsi—powerful beings who embody sensual enjoyment, revenge, and wrath; rājasāḥ—those in the mode of passion; pretān-bhūta-gaṇān—ghosts and spirits; cha—and; anye—others; yajante—worship; tāmasāḥ—those in the mode of ignorance; janāḥ—persons'),
('035821de-6113-5553-ad55-c8a3c280dda2'::uuid, 17, 5, 600, 600, 'अशास्त्रविहितं घोरं तप्यन्ते ये तपो जनाः।दम्भाहङ्कारसंयुक्ताः कामरागबलान्विताः।।17.5।।', 'aśhāstra-vihitaṁ ghoraṁ tapyante ye tapo janāḥ
dambhāhankāra-sanyuktāḥ kāma-rāga-balānvitāḥ', '[{"word":"aśhāstra","meaning":"vihitam—not enjoined by the scriptures"},{"word":"ghoram","meaning":"stern"},{"word":"tapyante","meaning":"perform"},{"word":"ye","meaning":"who"},{"word":"tapaḥ","meaning":"austerities"},{"word":"janāḥ","meaning":"people"},{"word":"dambha","meaning":"hypocrisy"},{"word":"ahankāra","meaning":"egotism"},{"word":"sanyuktāḥ","meaning":"possessed of"},{"word":"kāma","meaning":"desire"},{"word":"rāga","meaning":"attachment"},{"word":"bala","meaning":"force"},{"word":"anvitāḥ","meaning":"impelled by"}]'::jsonb, 'aśhāstra-vihitam—not enjoined by the scriptures; ghoram—stern; tapyante—perform; ye—who; tapaḥ—austerities; janāḥ—people; dambha—hypocrisy; ahankāra—egotism; sanyuktāḥ—possessed of; kāma—desire; rāga—attachment; bala—force; anvitāḥ—impelled by;')
